RODE
====

Run `rode` or launch RODE from your desktop's Development menu.
Open a local project with `rode /path/to/project`.
Connect over SSH with `rode --ssh user@host --remote-path '~/project'`.

The package includes the static rode-sessiond helper for persistent local/SSH
terminals. Remote file access requires Python 3 on the remote host. Optional
features use installed project-host tools; configure them inside RODE.

PDF previews use desktop Poppler tools (poppler-utils). Project sandboxing uses
bubblewrap when available; normal mode remains usable without it.
Encrypted projects require gocryptfs and working FUSE on the project host.
Use File -> Open encrypted project to create or unlock encrypted storage.

Documentation: https://pbenner.github.io/rode/
Source: https://github.com/pbenner/rode

Package installation/removal does not start or stop user terminal sessions,
alter user preferences, or deploy a system service. Restart the editor to use
new binaries, retaining persistent sessions when needed.
